course: dictionary
lesson: 10888
title: Violently: how something happens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An adverb tells you more about a verb: how, when or where something happens. «Violently» is an adverb, and it tells you how something was done. It comes from the word violent, and many adverbs end in -ly.
explain: «He pushed the door violently.» Look at the words around it. Pushed is the action, and violently tells us how hard he pushed. Try your meaning in the sentence: he pushed the door with strong force. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Violently can also mean very strongly or very much. «They disagreed violently» and «she was violently sick» do not mean anyone hit anything. The words around it show the feeling or the extreme degree.
explain: Watch for phrases like shake violently, react violently, violently ill and violently opposed. When you meet violently, ask yourself: is this about force, a sudden strong event, or an extreme feeling?
fact: Violently is an adverb, and it tells you how something happens.
fact: «Violently» can mean with strong physical force, as in «he pushed the door violently».
fact: «Violently» can also mean very strongly or suddenly, as in «the ground shook violently».
fact: «Violently» can mean very much, to an extreme degree, as in «they disagreed violently».
fact: Stars more than about 8 times as heavy as the Sun die violently in a supernova, an explosion that can outshine a whole galaxy for weeks.
exercise: «The volcano erupted violently and sent ash high into the sky.» What does violently tell us about the eruption? | *Strongly and suddenly | Slowly and quietly | Far away, over the sea | Without any noise
exercise: Which sentence uses violently to mean very much, to an extreme degree? | «The ground shook violently.» | «He pushed the gate violently.» | *«She was violently sick after the boat ride.»
exercise: Find and copy the one word in «Stars more than about 8 times as heavy as the Sun die violently in a supernova» that tells us how the stars die. | supernova | *violently | Sun | stars
test: «The sea rocked violently in the storm.» What does rocked violently suggest? | *Moved with strong, rough force | Stayed perfectly still | Sang a gentle song | Turned a bright colour
test: What does «met an untimely end» mean? | Had a very long, happy life | Won a race | *Died young or died violently | Moved house
exam: Jayden says violently always means loudly. Is he right? | Yes, violently always means a loud noise | No, it only means very slow and gentle | *No, it can mean strong force, sudden power or a very great degree | Yes, because it ends in -ly
